+# Lovable prompt 4.4, Working Calendar screens (lean), ready to paste
+
+This is Build Guide prompt 4.4, trimmed to fit the 100-credit budget (lean target of about 10 credits). The Excel template upload, its error preview and "copy to next year" are **deferred**. Enter the 2025 holidays by hand for the Workbook test data instead. The engine already has these endpoints (`GET /v1/calendar/template`, `POST /v1/calendar/clients/{client_id}/import`), so they can be added later in one small prompt.
+
+----------------------------------------------------------------
+Build Working Calendar: Federal holidays by year (provisional/confirmed, add, edit
+status, delete with reason); Emirate profiles; Client Work Week editor (Mon-Sun
+off-day toggles, half-day cut-off times, dated periods with overlap validation);
+Client exceptions (extra holiday / working day); colour-coded month preview. Show
+"Calendar used: {client} v{n}" on JE results and mark results STALE after changes.
+Log all changes.
+Use the engine paths already in src/lib/engine.ts: GET /v1/calendar/resolve
+(month preview), GET /v1/calendar/clients/{client_id}, POST
+/v1/calendar/clients/{client_id}/workweeks, POST
+/v1/calendar/clients/{client_id}/exceptions, POST /v1/calendar/emirate-profiles,
+POST /v1/calendar/holidays, PATCH /v1/calendar/holidays/{holiday_id}, and the DELETE
+paths. Only the user's own firm's clients are listed. Admin edits holidays and
+emirate profiles; Managers/Seniors edit their clients' work weeks and exceptions.
+Skip the Excel template upload and copy-to-next-year for now.
+----------------------------------------------------------------
